From: Alan Shearer
Subject: ipv4: free IP_MULTICAST_IF address in protocol destructor

IP_MULTICAST_IF stores a heap-allocated sockaddr in the IPv4
protocol object. The destructor deletes the raw socket wrapper but
does not release this address, leaking it when the socket is closed.

Delete multicast_address during protocol destruction.
ipv4_init_protocol() already sets the pointer to NULL, so a socket
that never set the option is safe.

---
 src/add-ons/kernel/network/protocols/ipv4/ipv4.cpp | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/src/add-ons/kernel/network/protocols/ipv4/ipv4.cpp b/src/add-ons/kernel/network/protocols/ipv4/ipv4.cpp
--- a/src/add-ons/kernel/network/protocols/ipv4/ipv4.cpp
+++ b/src/add-ons/kernel/network/protocols/ipv4/ipv4.cpp
@@ -172,6 +172,7 @@
 	~ipv4_protocol()
 	{
 		delete raw;
+		delete multicast_address;
 	}
 
 	RawSocket*			raw;
